      "Evidence": "The opening bedroom sequence and the mod-hub scene deliver real texture pull \u2014 the helix zipper pull, the Saltline foil animation, In\u00E9s\u0027s fern-light tattoos, the amber Thread pods \u2014 but the back half becomes a dense procedural of office paperwork, filing, invoices, and case-closing logistics that observes GLMZ\u0027s bureaucracy and horror mechanics without offering comparable sensory seduction.",
      "Fix": "Cut or compress the Rennick-office administrative stretch and redistribute its page-weight toward more strange-beautiful GLMZ texture (the flood-channel algae glow, the Thread pods, the mod-hub\u0027s living light) so allure keeps pace with the procedural horror throughout, not just in the first third."
